        "original_id": "e01476db-91d2-5dde-b842-6c458a0050f6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dan Lewis, Charlie Preedy\n- Organizations: Arsenal F.C., Cardiff City\n- Places: Highbury, London, England, Wales\n- Roles: football goalkeeper\n- Events: 1927 FA Cup Final\n- Topics: Arsenal goalkeeping\n\nFacts:\n- Dan Lewis was born on 11 December 1902 and was a Welsh football goalkeeper.\n- Dan Lewis is most notable for playing for Arsenal.\n- In the 1927 FA Cup Final, Dan Lewis kept goal for Arsenal, and a mistake by him led to Cardiff City winning the cup.\n- Arsenal Football Club is a professional football club based in Highbury, London, England.\n- Arsenal Football Club plays in the Premier League, the top flight of English football.\n- Charlie Preedy was initially not Arsenal's first-team goalkeeper and mainly played as understudy to Dan Lewis, Arsenal's regular goalkeeper.\n- Dan Lewis died in 1965.",
